  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aawaz II: Inclusion, Accountability and Preventing Modern Slavery - Coordination, Monitoring and Reporting (UNJP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing technical assistance to target government institutions to improve legislation, systems, policies and data on vulnerable or excluded groups. Specifically:
o	Provision of technical assistance on legislation and policy reform, including:
To progress legislation relating to the prevention of modern slavery, for instance prevention of early/forced marriage, domestic violence and improved child labour legislation.
-  To support national and provincial partners, including the Ministry of Human Rights and provincial Women&#x2019;s Development Departments, to roll out action plans to implement gender equality and violence against women policy reform.
o	Institutional strengthening in strategically important bodies, including:
Provide technical guidance to relevant provincial/regional institutions (including the National and Provincial Commissions for the Status for Women (NCSW, PCSW)) to leverage resources for effective planning, financing and delivery of progressive legislation, policy and budgeting for vulnerable groups. 
- Technical assistance to build the Government of Pakistan&#x2019;s data collection capacity, including support to the provincial Bureaux of Statistics and Labour Departments for the implementation of SIMPOC  household-based child labour surveys. 
- Systems building with the relevant provincial departments to put in place mechanisms to more effectively register births and to receive monitor and investigate cases of child abuse and exploitation .  
o	Technical assistance provided to provincial governments to develop government funded Youth Action Plans to implement provincial youth policies, in consultation with young people.
&#x2022; Growing the evidence base for action through evaluation of programme outcomes and evidence generation/dissemination in the areas of gender, youth, religious minorities, disabilities and modern slavery. Knowledge products could include: 
o	National VAWG prevalence survey in line with CEDAW and SDG monitoring requirements</narrative>
  </description>
